.TH "frontend/node_modules/@nodelib/fs.scandir Directory Reference" 3 "Version 0.1" "Chat-ME!" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/@nodelib/fs.scandir Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "@nodelib/fs\&.scandir"
.PP
.RS 4
List files and directories inside the specified directory\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SH ":bulb: Highlights"
.PP
The package is aimed at obtaining information about entries in the directory\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
:moneybag: Returns useful information: \fRname\fP, \fRpath\fP, \fRdirent\fP and \fRstats\fP (optional)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
:gear: On Node\&.js 10\&.10+ uses the mechanism without additional calls to determine the entry type\&. See \fB`old` and `modern` mode\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
:link: Can safely work with broken symbolic links\&.
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install @nodelib/fs\&.scandir
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
import * as fsScandir from '@nodelib/fs\&.scandir';

fsScandir\&.scandir('path', (error, stats) => { /* … */ });
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "\&.scandir(path, [optionsOrSettings], callback)"
Returns an array of plain objects (\fB`Entry`\fP) with information about entry for provided path with standard callback-style\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
fsScandir\&.scandir('path', (error, entries) => { /* … */ });
fsScandir\&.scandir('path', {}, (error, entries) => { /* … */ });
fsScandir\&.scandir('path', new fsScandir\&.Settings(), (error, entries) => { /* … */ });
.fi
.PP
.SS "\&.scandirSync(path, [optionsOrSettings])"
Returns an array of plain objects (\fB`Entry`\fP) with information about entry for provided path\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const entries = fsScandir\&.scandirSync('path');
const entries = fsScandir\&.scandirSync('path', {});
const entries = fsScandir\&.scandirSync(('path', new fsScandir\&.Settings());
.fi
.PP
.SS "path"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Required: \fRtrue\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRstring | Buffer | URL\fP
.PP

.PP
A path to a file\&. If a URL is provided, it must use the \fRfile:\fP protocol\&.
.SS "optionsOrSettings"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Required: \fRfalse\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fROptions | Settings\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: An instance of \fRSettings\fP class
.PP

.PP
An \fB`Options`\fP object or an instance of \fB`Settings`\fP class\&.

.PP
.RS 4
:book: When you pass a plain object, an instance of the \fRSettings\fP class will be created automatically\&. If you plan to call the method frequently, use a pre-created instance of the \fRSettings\fP class\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SS "Settings([options])"
A class of full settings of the package\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const settings = new fsScandir\&.Settings({ followSymbolicLinks: false });

const entries = fsScandir\&.scandirSync('path', settings);
.fi
.PP
.SH "Entry"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRname\fP — The name of the entry (\fRunknown\&.txt\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRpath\fP — The path of the entry relative to call directory (\fRroot/unknown\&.txt\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdirent\fP — An instance of \fR\fRfs\&.Dirent\fP\fP class\&. On Node\&.js below 10\&.10 will be emulated by \fR\fRDirentFromStats\fP\fP class\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRstats\fP (optional) — An instance of \fRfs\&.Stats\fP class\&.
.PP

.PP
For example, the \fRscandir\fP call for \fRtools\fP directory with one directory inside:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
    dirent: Dirent { name: 'typedoc', /* … */ },
    name: 'typedoc',
    path: 'tools/typedoc'
}
.fi
.PP
.SH "Options"
.PP
.SS "stats"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRboolean\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRfalse\fP
.PP

.PP
Adds an instance of \fRfs\&.Stats\fP class to the \fB`Entry`\fP\&.

.PP
.RS 4
:book: Always use \fRfs\&.readdir\fP without the \fRwithFileTypes\fP option\&. ??TODO?? 
.RE
.PP
.SS "followSymbolicLinks"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRboolean\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRfalse\fP
.PP

.PP
Follow symbolic links or not\&. Call \fRfs\&.stat\fP on symbolic link if \fRtrue\fP\&.
.SS "\fRthrowErrorOnBrokenSymbolicLink\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRboolean\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRtrue\fP
.PP

.PP
Throw an error when symbolic link is broken if \fRtrue\fP or safely use \fRlstat\fP call if \fRfalse\fP\&.
.SS "\fRpathSegmentSeparator\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fRstring\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRpath\&.sep\fP
.PP

.PP
By default, this package uses the correct path separator for your OS (\fR\\\fP on Windows, \fR/\fP on Unix-like systems)\&. But you can set this option to any separator character(s) that you want to use instead\&.
.SS "\fRfs\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: \fR\fRFileSystemAdapter\fP\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: A default FS methods
.PP

.PP
By default, the built-in Node\&.js module (\fRfs\fP) is used to work with the file system\&. You can replace any method with your own\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
interface FileSystemAdapter {
    lstat?: typeof fs\&.lstat;
    stat?: typeof fs\&.stat;
    lstatSync?: typeof fs\&.lstatSync;
    statSync?: typeof fs\&.statSync;
    readdir?: typeof fs\&.readdir;
    readdirSync?: typeof fs\&.readdirSync;
}

const settings = new fsScandir\&.Settings({
    fs: { lstat: fakeLstat }
});
.fi
.PP
.SH "\fRold\fP and \fRmodern\fP mode"
.PP
This package has two modes that are used depending on the environment and parameters of use\&.
.SS "old"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Node\&.js below \fR10\&.10\fP or when the \fRstats\fP option is enabled
.PP

.PP
When working in the old mode, the directory is read first (\fRfs\&.readdir\fP), then the type of entries is determined (\fRfs\&.lstat\fP and/or \fRfs\&.stat\fP for symbolic links)\&.
.SS "modern"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Node\&.js 10\&.10+ and the \fRstats\fP option is disabled
.PP

.PP
In the modern mode, reading the directory (\fRfs\&.readdir\fP with the \fRwithFileTypes\fP option) is combined with obtaining information about its entries\&. An additional call for symbolic links (\fRfs\&.stat\fP) is still present\&.

.PP
This mode makes fewer calls to the file system\&. It's faster\&.
